  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Coastal & Oceanic Plankton Ecology, Production & Observation Database (COPEPOD)",
  "description": "Coastal & Oceanic Plankton Ecology, Production & Observation Database (COPEPOD) is a global plankton database. COPEPOD offers in situ zooplankton and phytoplankton abundance, biomass, and composition data at three processing levels: Level 1) Data Subsets containing data and summaries based on the original cruise, project, or institute data collections; Level 2) Data Compilations containing a compiled collections of all data within COPEPOD for various taxonomic groups; and Level 3) Data Products containing calculated mean fields of annual and seasonal mean biomass or abundance. [Reference: O'Brien, T.D. 2004. COPEPOD: The Coastal & Oceanic Plankton Ecology, Production & Observation Database [Online]. Available: http://www.st.nmfs.noaa.gov/plankton.]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: COPEPOD is an effort by NOAA - National Marine Fisheries Service (NMFS) to provide investigators with an integrated data set of quality-controlled, globally distributed plankton abundance, biomass and composition data, along with co-sampled environmental data. COPEPOD is designed to help the investigator easily see exactly what data are currently available and then download it in a usable format. In additional to data distribution maps, COPEPOD offers a variety of content summaries and searching options.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23568426",
